module gunbc.guarantee_stall.let_bound_closure_parameters_are_emitted_without_their_declared_types_stall

import gunbc.guarantee_rung { Mitigatable, MechanicallyPreventable }
import gunbc.guarantee_stall { GuaranteeStall, BoundedPopulation, climbs_when }
import gunbc.rung_climb { ClimbableButUnbuilt }

// A STALL, NOT A DROP -- and the difference is measured, not stylistic. gunbc.guarantee_stall is explicit
// that a DROP is an event (something held a rung and stopped holding it) while a STALL is a standing state
// (a class sits below its attainable ceiling and has not moved), and that forcing previous/temporary/reason
// onto a class that never held the higher rung "would fabricate an event that did not happen". That is the
// state of this population. On origin/main 2026-11-27, `git log -S'elem_type_str: "_"' -- src/v1/05_emit_rust.dag`
// returns exactly ONE commit, b432cf1e5f0 ("typed let-bound lambdas (emit)", #12307) -- the commit that
// introduced the arm. Across the whole history of that file the ExprLambda arm has exactly one spelling,
// `ExprLambda => emit_typed_collection_lambda(lambda_expr: value, elem_type_str: "_", ...)`. So the let-bound
// path has never emitted a typed parameter annotation, no executed observation of one exists at any earlier
// tree, and there is no fall to record. This row was first authored as a gunbc.rung_drop on 2026-11-27; five
// reviews refused that carrier and neat-badger-614 ruled on 2026-11-27, citing the guarantee ladder ("a class's
// rung is the minimum across its in-scope paths") and guarantee_stall's own text ("Those rows are
// gunbc.guarantee_stall now"), that it belongs here. No operator escalation was made for this row; no
// gunbc.design_ruling entry is claimed by it and no operator words exist to record.
//
// WHAT IS STALLING, AND WHOSE REPAIR IT HOLDS BACK. The repair of roadmap row
// emission-ownership-facts-survive-lowering requires the five arms of emission-building-block-realization to
// reach their declared output for the let-bound-closure subject family. Those five arms -- the population
// below -- each produce an instrument subject whose emitter output is a let-bound Rust closure, and the
// emitter writes those closures without parameter type annotations, so rustc answers E0282 at the emit-compile
// leg. The subject's declared formal types exist and are readable at the binding site; what is missing is the
// wiring that carries them into the emitted parameter annotation.
//
// WHY CURRENT IS MITIGATABLE, argued from what held rather than from what could be done. Current is the rung
// the let-bound path establishes by EXECUTED evidence, and the executed evidence is an emission that fails: on
// srv1, slot 9 acquired 2026-11-27T14:22:15Z, BOOT c095c0cd, head 435289c1c1129dbb3add4d4d12cc3063b20c84a0,
// the accumulator-observation instrument emitted a let-bound closure without annotations --
// "let scale = |x: _| v1_rt::int_add(acc_int_identity(x.clone()), 1);" -- and rustc refused with 3 error[E0282]
// among 5 errors total, first at subjects.rs:138:60, the acc_local_closure scale binding. At this rung nothing
// inside the emitter prevents the bad output: v1.compiler.emit_rust::emit_typed_let's ExprLambda arm supplies
// the "_" fallback unconditionally and v1.compiler.emit_rust::lambda_param_type_strs renders it verbatim when
// the parameter node resolves to nothing, so the refusal comes from a downstream consumer (rustc), not from a
// check on the emitter's own output. The available worker action is observation and reporting: name the hole
// at the leg where it fires and carry it. That is Mitigatable's content, and it is what the executed leg
// demonstrated.
//
// WHY CEILING IS MECHANICALLY PREVENTABLE, argued from a path where that rung HOLDS, not from a capability
// nobody built. The emitter already owns a mechanism that mechanically prevents untyped closure parameters,
// and it is executing on a sibling path today. In src/v1/05_emit_rust.dag, v1.compiler.emit_rust::
// emit_rust_fold_method_call derives lambda_acc_type_str and fold_elem_type_str from the fold call's resolved
// types and passes them to v1.compiler.emit_rust::emit_typed_fold_lambda, which hands them to
// v1.compiler.emit_rust::lambda_param_type_strs as fallback_types with fold_acc_uses_fallback set, so each
// fold parameter renders with a declared type wherever inference yields none -- with no expected-type context
// and no human check in the loop. Re-measured on origin/main 2026-11-27 by
// `git grep -cE '\|acc: [A-Za-z_]' origin/main -- src/`: 588 matching lines across 64 files, spanning the
// emitter source, the emitted seed folds, and tests that assert the emitted fold closures carry typed
// parameters (src/v1/compiler_tests_rust.dag asserts the emitted route contains "fold(walk_init(),
// |acc: Rc<Walk>, ...)"). MechanicallyPreventable is therefore the ceiling of this class rather than an
// aspiration: the same emitter, for the same parameter-annotation obligation, prevents the failure wherever
// the mechanism is wired. Per gunbc.design_argument::guarantee_ladder the class's rung is the MINIMUM across
// its in-scope paths, so the five let-bound subjects sit at Mitigatable while the fold path holds the ceiling,
// and the ceiling is not lowered to make the row read conservatively -- the fold path's evidence is kept, and
// it is the reason the row is a stall with a named climb rather than a permanent state.
//
// WHY THE BLOCKER IS ClimbableButUnbuilt and NOT AwaitsOneGrounding. Nothing has to be declared first: the
// capability the climb needs is already authored, named and executing in the same file (emit_typed_fold_lambda's
// resolved-type path above), and the emitter's own comment beside it records the one design constraint on the
// repair -- "THE FIRST ATTEMPT AT THIS CHANGED THE FALLBACK TYPE STRING AND MEASURED NO EFFECT:
// lambda_param_type_strs prefers the parameter node's own RESOLVED type and only falls back when there is none
// ... The override has to sit where the parameter string is chosen, not where the fallback is supplied." What
// is missing is the wiring of that existing mechanism to the let-binding arm. That is unbuilt work on a
// demonstrated capability, which is ClimbableButUnbuilt's content; AwaitsOneGrounding would claim a
// declaration is absent, and none is.
//
// WHAT IS NOT IN THIS ROW'S POPULATION, and the same census so a reader can re-derive it. The untyped-fallback
// shape "item: _|" appears 3 times under src/ by `git grep -n ': _|' origin/main -- src/`, all three in the
// emitter's own seed source at src/v1/stage0/src/v1_compiler_infer.rs (two in v1_compiler_infer::realization_names,
// one in v1_compiler_infer::realization_declared_names). Those are hand-written seed folds that leave the
// element parameter to inference; they are not instrument subjects, they compile, and they are not members of
// this population. Only the five arms named below are, because only they are observed failing.
data let_bound_closure_parameters_are_emitted_without_their_declared_types_stall: GuaranteeStall = GuaranteeStall {
  subject: "the emitter's let-binding path emits a let-bound closure's parameters without their declared formal types, so the emitted Rust does not compile without an expected-type context (rustc E0282 at the emit-compile leg), while the same emitter annotates the sibling fold path mechanically; carried for the repair of emission-ownership-facts-survive-lowering and the five let-bound-closure arms of emission-building-block-realization",
  current: Mitigatable,
  ceiling: MechanicallyPreventable,
  blocker: ClimbableButUnbuilt,
  population: BoundedPopulation { members: [
    "acc_local_closure",
    "acc_local_closure_identity_only",
    "acc_local_closure_materializes_per_step",
    "acc_local_closure_escaping_closure",
    "acc_local_closure_copies_context"
  ] },
  next_rung_trigger: climbs_when(capability: "v1.compiler.emit_rust::emit_typed_let resolves each let-bound closure parameter's declared formal type at its ExprLambda arm and threads it through v1.compiler.emit_rust::emit_typed_collection_lambda into v1.compiler.emit_rust::lambda_param_type_strs at the point where that function chooses the parameter string -- not by replacing the fallback string alone, which its own comment records as measuring no effect -- replacing the elem_type_str: \"_\" that arm has passed since its single introducing commit b432cf1e5f0, so that the emitted Rust for all five members compiles with no expected-type context and the emit-compile leg returns no E0282. Rerunning the same instrument unchanged retires nothing, because it reproduces the same E0282 at the emit-compile leg; and hand-writing Rust parameter annotations in the emitted file retires nothing, because the emitted file is seed Rust and is outside every worker's authority on this lane. A default or timed-out closure of any ask is not a ruling.")
}
